    "verdict": "The atomic-model route is SCATTERED on the MATCHED (marginalized) comparison, not a single offset: obs/pred geo-SD 9.9x and range 805x for the marginalized+band prediction, 6.0x / 180x for marginalized-only, and 13.8x / 1997x for the known-pose upper bound. Marginalization does NOT rescue it -- every convention stays at geo-SD 6-13x, against the reconstructed-MAP route's 1.38x. Root cause (robust to the bank): a deposited atomic PAIR is an unreliable proxy for the real scored difference -- slco2a1's two models differ by only 0.42 A Ca yet the data separates them (obs >> pred), while cas9/slc19a3's large rigid motions overshoot. Compounding it, the K^-2/3 extrapolation was REFUSED for every system (K* unreachable), so there is no converged atomic marginalized d'^2 at feasible banks at all. Structure predicts real d'^2 reliably only through the map/FSC forward route, not the atomic shortcut (Eq. 1).",
    "note_convergence": "The real measurement used a large bank (score_pool fixed_bank ~4e6) and sits near-converged (obs/known_pose_map ~0.21 is an envelope factor, not a bank collapse), so the known-pose-band comparison (geo-SD 12.7x) is the most appropriate matched read; the base-bank marginals here (pose_eff 0.5-3.6%) are deep lower bounds. All conventions agree the route is scattered.",
